From 875e23850d0cfa38da047a5c38ee023c0f136c3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:52:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lexer: call unput() in cfg_dummy_function

cfg_dummy_function() calls yyunput(0, NULL) to stop the compiler
warning that the static yyunput() is defined but not used. flex 2.6.9
now defines yyunput as a one argument macro around yyunput_r(), so
the call fails to build:

  lexer.l:339:20: error: macro 'yyunput' passed 2 arguments, but takes just 1

Use the documented unput() macro instead, which every flex version
maps onto its unput function with the current text pointer.
---
 src/lexer.l | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/lexer.l b/src/lexer.l
index 8fd5ec8ed6c0..fcf062c2c4f3 100644
--- a/src/lexer.l
+++ b/src/lexer.l
@@ -336,7 +336,7 @@ void cfg_dummy_function(void)
     /* please compiler :-)
      * otherwise "defined but not used" warning
      */
-    yyunput(0, NULL);
+    unput(0);
 }
 
 static void cfg_raw_append(const char *s, int n)
-- 
2.53.0

